  "final": "Done. The cause was in `reorder_qty` in `inventory/stock.py`. It used floor division (`need // pack_size`), so it ordered too few packs whenever `need` wasn't an exact multiple of the pack size. I changed it to round up (`-(-need // pack_size)`).\n\n`python3 -m unittest` now exits 0 with all 7 tests passing. Before the fix it reported `FAILED (failures=183)`. The huge output came from one test (`test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack`) failing once for every `need` value from 1 to 199. For example, `192 not greater than or equal to 199`.\n\nI ran only that suite. The repo has no pytest installed, so I used unittest, as the README says.",
